# Third-party tools that live in the fleet's ~/.skenv next to the SK packages.
#
# Inventoried 2026-11-15 from `pip list --not-required` on the five fleet
# hosts' venvs. Not every host carries every tool: the rollout
# pins only the lock entries a host already has installed, so a tool listed here
# is not pushed onto a host that never had it. Listing it here is what makes its
# version part of the lock, so it can no longer conflict with an SK package
# silently (huggingface-hub vs skbrain's click cap, twine vs the rich<14 caps).
#
# Unpinned on purpose: the lock (deploy/fleet-constraints.txt) holds the
# versions, and scripts/fleet-lock.sh keeps every existing pin unless an input
# forces a change. Renovate moves them by PR.
#
# Left out: pip and setuptools (bootstrap), nvidia-* wheels (they arrive via
# torch), and stale SK leftovers no package requires any more (skcomm,
# cloud9-protocol, sklegal-calendar, skseal from git on one host).
aiohttp
ansible-core
black
boto3
# Security floors (CVE-2026-111497, GHSA-9v8h-qqgm-4m35, PYSEC-2026-4322/4323:
# out-of-bounds write in the Brotli decoder). No fleet host installs either one
# today; aiohttp, httpx and urllib3 pull them in through their brotli extras, so
# the floor keeps any host that gets one on a fixed release.
brotli>=1.2.1
brotlicffi>=1.2.1.0
